<title>USA: Hecla sells 3.95 mln shrs to Europe investors.</title>
<headline>Hecla sells 3.95 mln shrs to Europe investors.</headline>
<dateline>COEUR D'ALENE, Idaho 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hecla Mining Co said it agreed to sell 3.95 million shares of its common stock to European institutional investors at a price of $6.25 per share.</p>
<p>The company said it will use the money for its 1997 capital expenditures, mainly in connection with its Lucky Friday mine expansion in northern Idaho and its Rosebud gold project in Nevada.</p>
<p>After the sale, the company said it will have about 55 million outstanding common shares.</p>
</text>
